nodes.body:
@Nanfang-Li @UNIDY2002 Thanks, Nanfang, for reviewing and trying b919a57. I’d be happy to take the remote-worker case as a follow-up after the local-worker fix lands.

I saw the update to exit workers directly rather than use an error pipe. Our candidate was tested against the previous implementation, so I’ll need to check what remains necessary, adapt it to the revised design, and rerun validation before proposing it.

@UNIDY2002, would that split work for you, or would you prefer that we contribute the useful implementation and validation to #58738? I don’t want to assume your PR should be dropped. Our approach uses existing ZMQ disconnect notifications and cancellable response reads rather than a separate heartbeat channel.

The existing patch and results remain available above. Any revised submission would retain the AI-assistance disclosure and require my own review, relevant test runs, and sign-off.

@olivierzach Thanks for following up. I support pursuing the remote-worker/node failure follow-up from your ZMQ disconnect and cancellable response-read proposal.

It addresses the same multi-node failure gap as #58738 while reusing the existing control plane, so I agree that this is a better direction than maintaining a separate TCP heartbeat protocol. I will not continue the standalone protocol implementation in #58738.

Once it is adapted to the latest #53597 state, I can help validate it with the two-host remote-failure scenario and follow up on any remaining gaps.

